 "ISIC 4390 (Other specialized construction activities -- the residual
  specialized-construction-trade class: scaffolding erection, foundation-
  piling work, waterproofing and other specialty trade work not
  elsewhere classified, outside 4321 electrical / 4322 plumbing-heat-
  cool / 4329 other installation / 4330 completion-and-finishing) had a
  :spec-only placeholder pointing at a never-created
  gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-F4390 repo (gh api 404 confirmed at the real
  cloud-itonami org before any work began; live registry :name verified
  to match the assigned premise exactly: 'Other specialized construction
  activities'). Higher physical-risk trade domain than the
  4329/4330 insulation/finishing siblings -- scaffold-collapse and
  pile-driving-induced ground vibration can damage a NEIGHBORING
  structure, closer in public-safety stakes to the demolition/road-rail
  siblings this fleet's robotics-premise actors mirror structurally."
 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-4390 mirroring cloud-itonami-isic-4329
  (Other Construction Installation) / cloud-itonami-isic-4330 (Building
  Completion and Finishing) module-for-module: Specialized Trade Advisor
  ⊣ Specialized Trade Governor + audit ledger. Eight HARD gates: unknown
  op, effect-not-propose, forbidden action class (trade-equipment-
  control/direct-actuation/structural-completion-sign-off), site/permit-
  not-verified, legal-basis-missing, scaffold-inspection-incomplete,
  vibration-noncompliant, unresolved-safety-concern. MemStore/
  DatomicStore backends, fully portable .cljc with NO JVM interop
  anywhere in src/ (specialized.notify uses a caller-injected function
  transport seam instead of embedding java.net.http). No new Rust code,
  no robot-control code -- coordination-only, :itonami.blueprint/robotics
  false. UNLIKE 4329/4330 and LIKE 4311/4210:
  :schedule-specialized-operation IS a permanent high-stakes member --
  NEVER auto-commits at any phase, reflecting scaffold-collapse/pile-
  driving-vibration public-safety stakes materially closer to
  demolition/heavy-civil earthwork scheduling than to 4329/4330's
  insulation/finishing domain. Op named :schedule-specialized-operation,
  deliberately NOT reusing 4330's :schedule-finishing-operation name --
  domain mismatch (4390 is not building-completion/finishing work).
  Per-jurisdiction (JPN/USA/DEU) legal-basis catalog with TWO
  independent bases (scaffold-inspection + pile-driving-vibration,
  unlike 4329/4330's single hazmat+fall-protection pairing) -- every
  citation independently verified via WebSearch/WebFetch against
  laws.e-gov.go.jp / osha.gov / baua.de / dinmedia.de before being
  written. JPN (75 dB site-boundary vibration LEVEL, 振動規制法) and DEU
  (5 mm/s PEAK PARTICLE VELOCITY, DIN 4150-3 row-2 Anhaltswert) have
  real quantitative vibration triggers in their OWN native, genuinely
  DIFFERENT physical units -- never normalized to a shared unit. USA is
  honestly :qualitative for vibration (OSHA has no federal numeric
  construction-vibration standard, only the OSH Act §5(a)(1) General
  Duty Clause) -- a deliberately different jurisdiction landing on
  :qualitative than 4329's DEU case, reflecting the real regulatory
  landscape for this specific hazard rather than copying which
  jurisdiction was qualitative in a sibling actor."
